  "title": "Canal Nightmarket Kitchens",
  "rules": [
    "Select one of 48 workers. Knife, pot, navigator and wash tools can be exchanged; carried items and warmth transfer through native handoffs.",
    "Unload one ingredient from a finite-stock barge only while an adjacent worker assists. Knife/navigator tools take root; others take grain.",
    "Cut roots at boards. Two cut roots and one grain make broth; one cut root and two grain make a rice plate. A clean stove cooks for four ticks.",
    "Wash uses local water and restores a clean stove use. Open locks send water downstream through two FIFO slots; fresh water enters only at the west.",
    "Footbridges require water at most three; barges require water at least two and open locks. Barges and customer docks travel along the canal.",
    "Serve the requested dish while warm. Requests are local; relay them before committing ingredients. Nightmarket closes at 768."
  ],
